Subject: [PATCH KW1/3] key-web: register the unprivileged key-web:// scheme

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
Copyright 2026 The Key-Origin Web Authors
Target: Chromium 160.0.8176.0 (apply with: patch -p1 -d src < this.patch)

Registers key-web:// as a standard, secure, CORS-enabled, service-worker and
web-storage scheme, and makes it structurally impossible for it to become an
isolated context:

  * chrome/common/chrome_content_client.cc
      Adds key-web to kChromeStandardURLSchemes plus the secure, CORS, SW and
      web-storage lists. It is NOT added to isolated_app_schemes or
      csp_bypassing_schemes, and it IS added to the new
      never_isolated_context_schemes list.
  * content/public/common/content_client.h, content/common/url_schemes.cc
      New Schemes::never_isolated_context_schemes. RegisterContentSchemes()
      CHECKs that every entry is standard + secure and absent from
      isolated_app / csp_bypassing / extension / local / no_access /
      code_cache lists, and that it never reaches
      blink::CommonSchemeRegistry::RegisterURLSchemeAsIsolatedApp(). Because
      Blink only reports IsIsolatedContext() for schemes registered there,
      key-web documents always see IsIsolatedContext() == false.
  * chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
      ShouldUrlUseApplicationIsolationLevel() returns false for key-web (and
      blob:/filesystem: URLs whose inner origin is key-web) before any IWA
      logic runs, so key-web can reach kIsolated (COOP+COEP) but never
      kIsolatedApplication.
  * components/webapps/key_web/{scheme.h,key_web_origin.*}
      kKeyWebScheme and KeyWebOrigin: key-web://<kw-id>.key only. Name hosts
      (cool-site.alice.example), bare IDs, ports, userinfo and proxy-mode IDs
      are rejected. Partition domain = "k" + b64(SHA-256(ctx || origin)).
  * chrome/common/chrome_features.*: kKeyOriginWeb (disabled by default).
      Scheme registration precedes the FeatureList, so the feature gates the
      loader factory (KW3), not the scheme.

There is no //url in the 160.0.8176.0 reference checkout, and Chromium keeps
embedder schemes out of url/url_constants.h (isolated-app lives in
components/webapps/isolated_web_apps/scheme.h). kKeyWebScheme follows that
precedent in components/webapps/key_web/scheme.h.

Tests: components_unittests --gtest_filter='KeyWebOriginTest.*'

